title: SecondLoopWisteria1
tags:
---

<< if DoesHeKnow("WisteriaTarot") == true && $ThisLoopMetWisteria== false >> //Met her in a previous loop 
	SETTING - The great fountain in NAUKA SQUARE. Flags flutter in the wind. The parade sounds notably closer now. There is a doctor standing by the fountain.
	AT RISE -  THE DOCTOR gives SASHA a quick look up and down at the approach, then turns away again.
	NARRATOR: Dr. Wisteria looks the same as she did the last time you saw her. Disinterested.
    << if $ArtMajor == true >>
        Other than those bloodstains on her coat, her appearance is immaculate and well prepared.
        Half-black, half-soft-red lipstick. Brushed and neat hair. Every button on her coat is fastened. She created her image very purposely.
    << endif >>
    DR. WISTERIA: Oh good. I was worried nobody would get maimed on the day of the Parade. 
    DR. WISTERIA: So, what is wrong with you? 
<< elseif $ThisLoopMetWisteria == true >> // Already talked to her this loop 
	    DR. WISTERIA: Did I not tell you to leave? Go away.
    -> Leave
	<<stop>>
<< else >> //Haven’t met her at all yet
	SETTING - The great fountain in NAUKA SQUARE. Flags flutter in the wind. The parade sounds notably closer now. There is a doctor standing by the fountain.
	AT RISE -  THE DOCTOR gives SASHA a quick look up and down at the approach, then turns away again.
	NARRATOR: The id-card on her lapel says “Dr. Wisteria - General Practitioner - Star Hospital”. 
    NARRATOR: There are some dark red stains at the bottom of her coat that imply she may do some more practical medicine than just consulting.
    << if $ArtMajor == true >>
	    Half-black, half-soft-red lipstick. Brushed and neat hair. Every button on her coat is fastened. She has created her image very purposely.
    << endif >>
    DR. WISTERIA: Oh good. I was worried nobody would get maimed on the day of the Parade. 
    DR. WISTERIA: So, what is wrong with you?
	<< Learn WisteriaTarot >>
<< endif >> 
<< set $ThisLoopMetWisteria = true >>

-> "I have experienced a hallucination of living through this entire day until the world ended, then going back in time to the start of it."
    SASHA: "I have experienced a hallucination of living through this entire day until the world ended, then going back in time to the start of it."
    << set $FirstWisteriaOptionsPicked = 0 >>
	DR. WISTERIA: Yeah, I’ve had dreams like that before.
	DR. WISTERIA: You sound pretty distressed by it, though. I’ll take a look.
	DR. WISTERIA: Let’s see… Delusions, confusion, difficulty distinguishing reality from fiction…
-> "I just experienced the end of the world and then traveled back in time."
    SASHA: "I just experienced the end of the world and then traveled back in time."
    << set $FirstWisteriaOptionsPicked = 1 >>
	DR. WISTERIA: (silence)
	DR. WISTERIA: ..Let’s see… Delusions, confusion, difficulty distinguishing reality from fiction…
-> "I think there is something wrong with my brain."
    SASHA: "I think there is something wrong with my brain."
    << set $FirstWisteriaOptionsPicked = 2 >>
	DR. WISTERIA: Yeah, I noticed.
	DR. WISTERIA: Does your brain hurt you when you give comprehensive descriptions?
-> "Fabian told me to come here. I am very confused and I’m not sure what is going on."
    SASHA: "Fabian told me to come here. I am very confused and I’m not sure what is going on."
    << set $FirstWisteriaOptionsPicked = 3 >>
	DR. WISTERIA: How kind of him, offloading lost tourists to me.
	DR. WISTERIA: I’m going to assume you mean you got some brain problems going on, because otherwise there is not much we can do here.
	DR. WISTERIA: I can charge the consultation either way, so not my problem.


DR. WISTERIA: For now, I’m thinking we follow a standard psychological evaluation.
DR. WISTERIA: (readies a clipboard in a semi-interested manner)
DR. WISTERIA: First question, have you suffered any head trauma recently? 
-> "Yes"
    SASHA: "Yes."
    << set $SecondWisteriaOptionsPicked = 0 >>
-> "No"
    SASHA: "No."
    << set $SecondWisteriaOptionsPicked = 1 >>
-> "What?"
    SASHA: "What?"
    DR. WISTERIA: It means, did you get hit on the head recently? 
    DR. WISTERIA: Or as a child? That's the next question. You can answer that one in advance.
    -> "Yes"
        SASHA: "Yes."
        << set $SecondWisteriaOptionsPicked = 0 >>
    -> "No" 
        SASHA: "No."
        << set $SecondWisteriaOptionsPicked = 1 >>

<< if $PsychMajor == true >>
	PSYCH: Even as she writes, she's looking at you. It's a little frightening, like she can see through any of your lies-- if there were any.
<< elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
	ART: The way she scratches on her clipboard is grating. Seriously, press that pen down a little less hard, would you?
<< elseif $TechMajor == true >>
	TECH: Despite this air of disbelief she holds about her, she's noting everything down diligently.
<< endif >>

DR. WISTERIA: Second question: Do you have any psychological problems?
DR. WISTERIA: That means disorders, mental illness, or just general personality defects.

-> "Yes."
	SASHA: "Yes."
	<<set $SashaAutismDiagnosis = true>>
	DR. WISTERIA: This wasn't a yes or no question. I meant if you could actually name what you have.
	DR. WISTERIA: Whatever. I can take a guess at what you have.
        << if $PsychMajor == true >>
	        Judging by her impatient foot tapping, you suspect she wants to hurry this up. She does genuinely think that she has something better to be doing now, but you don’t discount the possibility that she just doesn't like you.
        << endif >>
-> "No."
	SASHA: "No."
	DR. WISTERIA: Good, less work to do. Or bad, if it means you have problems you are just now discovering. But that isn’t my problem.
-> "I think so?"
	SASHA: "I think so?"
	<<set $SashaAutismDiagnosis = true>>
	DR. WISTERIA: This wasn't a yes or no question. I meant if you could actually name what you have.
	DR. WISTERIA: Though if it had been a yes or no question, that would still have been a terrible answer.
	DR. WISTERIA: Whatever. I can take a guess at what you have.
-> "I’m an artist, does that count?" <<if $ArtMajor == true>>
	SASHA: "I’m an artist, does that count?"
	<< set $SashaNonAutismDiagnosis = true>>
	<<set $SashaAutismDiagnosis = true>>
    DR. WISTERIA: (unamused) No, it does not. But I'm marking down "Other/ Unidentified Mental Disorder” here.


DR. WISTERIA: Okay, do you have a history of delusions, hallucinations or other similar symptoms?
DR. WISTERIA: Actually, hold on. This form is going to take way too long like this. (hands SASHA the form)
DR. WISTERIA: You can fill yes or no on all the items on this list, then give me the form back.
NARRATOR: The first half of the form is filled out in a neat clinical handwriting. 
NARRATOR: “Patient name” is empty. You never did tell her your name, huh. It might be a little awkward to bring that up now.
//Depending on your previous answers:
<< if $FirstLoopWisteriaOptionsPicked == 0 >>
    NARRATOR: The first section says ”Symptoms: Hallucinations, confusion, disorientation, potential dyschronometria.”
<< elseif $FirstLoopWisteriaOptionsPicked == 1 >>
    NARRATOR: The first section says ”Symptoms: Vivid imagination”, followed by a little drawing of a stick figure stabbing itself in the head.
<< elseif $FirstLoopWisteriaOptionsPicked == 2 >>
    NARRATOR: The first section says ”Symptoms: Unclear. Possible disorientation, confusion.”
<< elseif $FirstLoopWisteriaOptionsPicked == 3 >>
    NARRATOR: The first section says ”Symptoms: Disorientation, confusion, general discomfort.”
<< endif >>

<< if $SecondLoopWisteriaOptionsPicked == 0 >>
    NARRATOR: It is followed by ”Recent head trauma, potential concussion”
<< elseif $SecondLoopWisteriaOptionsPicked == 1 >>
    NARRATOR: It is followed by “No recent head trauma. No physical signs of injury.”
<< endif >>

<<if $SashaAutismDiagnosis == true>>
	<< if $ArtMajor == true >>
		NARRATOR: She also wrote “Signs of unspecified developmental disorder, potentially Adult Autism. Not enough symptoms for diagnosis test. Brain damage cannot be sufficiently ruled out.” 
		<<if $SashaNonAutismDiagnosis == true>>
			NARRATOR: She really [i]did[/i] write “Other/ Unidentified Mental Disorder” too.
		<<endif>>
	<< else >>
		NARRATOR: She also wrote “Signs of unspecified developmental disorder, potentially Adult Autism. Not enough symptoms for diagnosis test. Brain damage cannot be sufficiently ruled out.”
	<< endif >>
<<endif>>

DR. WISTERIA: Don’t read the rest of the form, that’s not for you. Just fill in the list.
-> Fill in Yes on everything
    DR. WISTERIA: (Watches with a slight frown)
    DR. WISTERIA: You have had a real shitty life, huh? 
    DR. WISTERIA: Or.. you didn’t read any of this. 
    DR. WISTERIA: Considering you marked that you’ve been divorced with children, I think I can count all of this as “prefer not to say”.
-> Fill in No on everything
    DR. WISTERIA: (incredulous) Really? Nothing? What a perfect little life you’ve had.
DR. WISTERIA: Alright, that’s a wrap. I’ve got good news for you: You are discharged.
DR. WISTERIA: You can leave now.
-> "Wait, that's it?"
	SASHA: "Wait, that's it?"
    DR. WISTERIA: What exactly were you expecting? Nothing's hurting you, threatening you, or making you bleed. 
    DR. WISTERIA: Be thankful I indulged you enough to grab this form. If the results indicated you could be unstable or a danger to others I can give you a referral for one. 
    DR. WISTERIA: Unfortunately for you, you seem pretty normal to me. You won't get to go to the loony bin. Bummer.
    << if $PsychMajor == true >>
        PSY: In your own opinion as a psychology graduate, you’re quite sure that you haven’t gone insane too.
    << endif >>
        -> "I am unstable and dangerous, I swear!"
			SASHA: "I am unstable and dangerous, I swear!"
            DR. WISTERIA: You're a [i]great[/i] actor, I can almost believe it. 
            DR. WISTERIA: If you're trying to get me to prescribe you drugs-- you're barking up the wrong tree. As I said, not a psychologist. I can’t give you any of the fun ones.
            << if $PsychMajor == true >>
                PSY: She is wrong. Psychologists cannot prescribe medication. She means a psychiatrist. She certainly knows the distinction, and she certainly thinks that you don’t.
            << elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
                ART: What about morphine? She does surgery right? She definitely must have painkillers. There are many, many ‘fun’ drugs a doctor like her should have access to.
            << elseif $TechMajor == true >>
                TECH: Chemistry is not your expertise, but you don’t believe there is a drug that can negate the effects of ‘time travel’.
            << endif >>
-> "What are the results?"
	SASHA: "What are the results?"
    DR. WISTERIA: Nothing. Whatever you think happened to you doesn’t seem to have had any lingering effects.
	DR. WISTERIA: I can speculate on some potential causes, but without any more information or symptoms I can’t diagnose you with anything.
	DR. WISTERIA: I indulged you and your story, but if I actually go and I diagnose anything based on it, that would be close to medical malpractice.
	DR. WISTERIA: So you can leave and stop wasting the time of Solster’s most qualified medical practitioner now.
	DR. WISTERIA: I’m not a psychologist anyways, so unless you have actual physical brain worms in your head, I can’t do much for you.
    << if $PsychMajor == true >>
        PSY: You, on the other hand, [i]are[/i] a psychologist. You’re quite sure that you haven’t gone insane, or as sure as someone could possibly be.
        PSY: Whatever happened to you was not in your mind, at least not in the form of a mental illness. Even though she is being facetious, brain worms might not be that far-fetched.
    << endif >>
-> "What should I do now?"
	SASHA: "What should I do now?"
	DR. WISTERIA: I just told you. Do you want me to test your hearing too?
	DR. WISTERIA: You should be happy. You can just go live your life now, far away from me. Not everyone is so lucky.
    << if $ArtMajor == true >>
	    ART: She subtly closes her fist as she says this, gripping the table. There is a real anger behind her sarcasm, but it has nothing to do with you.
    << endif >>


-> "Is there anyone else I can talk to?"
	SASHA: "Is there anyone else I can talk to?"
    DR. WISTERIA: Yes, anybody else but me.


<< Learn DenizTarot>>
<< Learn DenizInfoB>> //works for wisteria
<< Learn WisteriaInfoB>>
DR. WISTERIA: (after a pause) If you want a second opinion, go bother Deniz. I’m sure they’ll be delighted to hear about your dreams that felt “so real”.
DR. WISTERIA: Now, leave.

===

